  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on qualitative expert consensus from a single workshop and survey, rather than a quantitative assessment of labor market demand or curriculum efficacy.",
      "what": "This study designed a workshop and distributed a pre-workshop survey to academic and industry experts to identify workforce development needs and educational obstacles in the field of connected and automated vehicles (CAVs). The investigation structured its findings around four core themes: next-generation infrastructure, human factors, modeling and simulation, and travel behavior.",
      "why": "It shifts the academic focus from purely researching CAV impacts to actively preparing the future transportation workforce, establishing a structured agenda for updating university curricula to match rapid private-sector technological advancements."
    }
